Keep an OpenSSH config's paths POSIX ones on POSIX.

ConvertPathFromOpenssh turns the forward slashes of an OpenSSH config's
paths into backslashes (GetNormalizedPath), as Windows' dialogs want them.
On POSIX that breaks the path: an imported site's IdentityFile
~/.ssh/id_ed25519 became \home\user\.ssh\id_ed25519, a file that does not
exist. The platform's delimiter tells the two apart in one expression both
compilers take: a backslash on Windows, so upstream's behaviour is
unchanged. Line counts are unchanged.

--- a/source/core/SessionData.cpp
+++ b/source/core/SessionData.cpp
@@ -1681,1 +1681,1 @@
-  UnicodeString Result = GetNormalizedPath(Path);
+  UnicodeString Result = (PathDelim == L'\\') ? GetNormalizedPath(Path) : ExcludeTrailingBackslash(Path);
